          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Integration
            is a process by which local data over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            or similar is
            %em accumulated
            to an
            = succeed "." do
              %em integral
          %p
            In its simplest form, this is a limiting notion of the process of forming
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sums"} sums
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+integration"} Riemann integration
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lebesgue+integration"} Lebesgue integration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            on a space against a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure"} measure
            which indicates, roughly, how much a local contribution of the function contributes to the whole accumulation process. Direct variants and refinements of this kind of integration is
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+of+differential+forms"} integration of differential forms
            and similar.
          %p
            The integration of differential forms induces a more general notion of integration, namely
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+in+differential+cohomology"} integration in differential cohomology
            and hence
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+in+generalized+cohomology"} integration in generalized cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure"} measure
            is replaced by a choice of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation in generalized cohomology
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th analytic integration
                %th cohomological integration
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure"} measure
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation in generalized cohomology
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lebesgue+integration"}> Lebesgue integration
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+of+differential+forms"} of differential forms
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/push-forward+in+generalized+cohomology"}> push-forward in generalized cohomology
                  \/
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+differential+cohomology"} in differential cohomology
          %h2#terminology Terminology
          %p
            The quantity whose integral we are taking is the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong integrand
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure"} measure
            %strong value
            of the integral. The
            %strong integral
            itself may be thought of as its value, but also (especially if this value fails to exist as we would like) could mean the entire expression. (Contrast this with the case of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/series"} series
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_a^b f(x) \,\mathrm{d}x
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \,\mathrm{d}x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi a
